<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<task id="050" project="spaarkeai-compose-r7">
  <metadata>
    <title>Async ProjectForMount with PDF fork — server parity with LoadAsync (FR-06)</title>
    <phase>5 PDF Import Parity (UC-7)</phase>
    <gate>passed</gate>
    <status>completed</status>
    <rigor>FULL</rigor>
    <rigor-reason>Modifies BFF .cs; a documented contract change (sync→async) with an Azure DI call on the mount path.</rigor-reason>
    <model-tier>opus</model-tier>
    <model-tier-reason>BFF contract change — ProjectForMount was deliberately synchronous/no-I/O per ADR-007/013; making it async is architectural and touches every caller. High blast radius.</model-tier-reason>
    <effort>high</effort>
    <parallel-group>none</parallel-group>
    <parallel-safe>false</parallel-safe>
    <parallel-reason>Touches ComposeService.cs ProjectForMount + all its callers (shared Compose spine / BFF; cross-worktree contention).</parallel-reason>
    <deps>001</deps>
    <tags>bff-api, api, backend, ai</tags>
    <estimated-effort>3-4 hours</estimated-effort>
  </metadata>

  <prompt>
    Give ProjectForMount@305–323 the same IsPdfSource → ProjectPdfToDocxAsync fork that LoadAsync already has (@502–508). This
    makes ProjectForMount async (an Azure Document-Intelligence DI call). Copy the LoadAsync PDF fork; keep the docx path
    synchronous-fast. Update all callers to await. Document the sync→async contract change in code + PR (NFR-04).
  </prompt>

  <role>SPAARKE platform developer. Expert in the Compose projection path, async refactoring, and Azure Document Intelligence. Follow ADRs strictly.</role>

  <goal>
    ProjectForMount is async and forks a PDF source to ProjectPdfToDocxAsync (mirroring LoadAsync@502–508), while the docx path
    stays synchronous-fast; all callers await; the contract change is documented in code + PR.
  </goal>

  <context>
    <background>
      spec.md FR-06 (UC-7) server half + NFR-04. LoadAsync already has the PDF fork; ProjectForMount does not, so a PDF cannot
      become an editable Compose doc via the mount path. Reuse R6's ComposePdfModelProjector / ProjectPdfToDocxAsync — do not re-build.
    </background>
    <relevant-files>
      <file role="modify">src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Services/Compose/ComposeService.cs</file>
      <file role="modify">src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Api/ComposeEndpoints.cs</file>
      <file role="canonical-reference">ComposeService.cs LoadAsync PDF branch @502–508 (IsPdfSource → ProjectPdfToDocxAsync) — copy this fork into ProjectForMount</file>
      <file role="canonical-reference">ComposeService.cs ProjectForMount@305–323 (the sync method to make async) + ComposeEndpoints.cs project@76</file>
    </relevant-files>
    <dependencies>
      <dependency task="001" status="pending">Coordination gate + publish-size baseline + DI-gate env confirmation.</dependency>
    </dependencies>
  </context>

  <constraints>
    <constraint source="ADR-007">ProjectForMount was deliberately synchronous / no-I/O per ADR-007/ADR-013 (NFR-04 tension). This task takes ADR Tensions path A: making it async for the PDF fork is a documented, project-scoped exception — the docx path MUST stay synchronous-fast (no added I/O).</constraint>
    <constraint source="ADR-013">Reuse R6's ProjectPdfToDocxAsync / ComposePdfModelProjector; MUST NOT re-build the PDF projector or add a new AI capability/playbook.</constraint>
    <constraint source="ADR-032">The PDF fork rides the existing compound-gated intake (NullComposePdfIntakeSource fallback); this task does not change the gate, only consumes it.</constraint>
    <constraint source="project">BFF change — state a Placement Justification in the PR (cite .claude/constraints/bff-extensions.md); work stays in Services/Compose/. Verify compressed publish size ≤60 MB and report delta vs the 001 baseline (~44.96 MB net10) — flag if ≥+5 MB; confirm no new HIGH CVE; run /conflict-check before the BFF PR.</constraint>
    <constraint source="project">Add a seam test (tests/integration/seam/**) for async ProjectForMount PDF projection (ADR-038). MUST NOT delete docxBridge.ts.</constraint>
  </constraints>

  <knowledge>
    <topic>compose projection, async contract, pdf fork</topic>
    <files>
      <file>.claude/adr/ADR-007-spefilestore.md</file>
      <file>.claude/adr/ADR-013-ai-architecture.md</file>
      <file>.claude/adr/ADR-032-bff-nullobject-kill-switch.md</file>
      <file>.claude/adr/ADR-049-compose-shadow-document.md</file>
      <file>.claude/constraints/bff-extensions.md</file>
      <file>docs/adr/ADR-038-testing-strategy.md</file>
      <file>projects/spaarkeai-compose-r7/spec.md</file>
    </files>
  </knowledge>

  <steps mode="directional">
    <step order="0" name="Context + rigor declaration">Declare rigor FULL, model-tier opus; load ADR-007/013 + spec FR-06 + LoadAsync fork reference.</step>
    <step order="1">Copy the LoadAsync PDF fork (@502–508) into ProjectForMount@305–323; make the method async; keep the docx path synchronous-fast.</step>
    <step order="2">Update all callers (ComposeEndpoints.cs project@76 and any others) to await.</step>
    <step order="3">Add a seam test proving PDF projection via ProjectForMount; verify docx path unchanged.</step>
    <step order="4">Document the sync→async contract change in code comments + PR (NFR-04, ADR Tensions path A).</step>
    <step order="5">Run publish-size + CVE checks; record delta vs 001 baseline in notes/.</step>
    <step order="6">Run xUnit + seam suites; verify green.</step>
    <step order="7">Update TASK-INDEX.md: set 050 status to ✅.</step>
    <step order="8">Document any deviation in projects/spaarkeai-compose-r7/notes/.</step>
  </steps>

  <escalation>
    <trigger>If the ProjectPdfToDocxAsync contract or the DI gate differs from the LoadAsync fork (e.g., a different projector signature), STOP and escalate (root §6 / §6.5) rather than adapting the async contract on the fly — the sync→async change is already a documented exception and further deviation needs sign-off.</trigger>
  </escalation>

  <tools>
    <tool name="dotnet">Build/test + publish-size measure for the BFF</tool>
  </tools>

  <outputs>
    <output type="code">src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Services/Compose/ComposeService.cs</output>
    <output type="code">src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Api/ComposeEndpoints.cs</output>
    <output type="test">tests/integration/seam/** async ProjectForMount PDF projection</output>
  </outputs>

  <acceptance-criteria>
    <criterion testable="true">Given a PDF source, when ProjectForMount runs, then it forks to ProjectPdfToDocxAsync (mirroring LoadAsync@502–508) and returns an editable projection.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">The docx path remains synchronous-fast (no added I/O); all callers await the now-async method.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">The sync→async contract change is documented in code + PR (NFR-04).</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Compressed publish size ≤60 MB with delta reported vs the 001 baseline; no new HIGH CVE.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">The seam test for async ProjectForMount PDF projection passes; xUnit green.</criterion>
  </acceptance-criteria>

  <notes>spec.md FR-06 server half, NFR-04, ADR Tensions row 2 (path A). Client gates + env verify + parity acceptance is task 051.</notes>

  <execution><skill>.claude/skills/task-execute/SKILL.md</skill></execution>
</task>
